{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1456797-how-do-camarilla-brujah-repair-the-results-of-their-clan-compulsion","id":1456797,"title":"How do Camarilla Brujah repair the results of their Clan Compulsion?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-08-13T22:47:30-07:00","id":1456797,"title":"How do Camarilla Brujah repair the results of their Clan Compulsion?","content":"During the centuries when Brujah were Camarilla, presumably Brujah periodically suffered their Clan Compulsion during highly inappropriate moments, such as when in Elysium or chatting with the Prince. How did they repair the results of this happening? It's kind of a problem if you are a Primogen or Sheriff, or simply a citizen attempting to remain in good standing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T02:57:38-07:00","id":1456802,"title":"","content":"I imagine a public apology would generally suffice, provided they didn't fuck anything up too badly and didn't piss off the local prince too much. Sometimes by &quot;going against orders&quot; things would turn out for the better and which case they could act smug and say, &quot;I told you so.&quot; In the event you pissed someone very important off badly enough and apology wasn't sufficient, then congrats, you might have been banned from Elysium, your Territory was taken away or you've basically just been declared persona non grata and de-facto forced to join the local Anarchs.<br /> <br /> This would likely one reason why the Brujah ended up being the Anarch clan. Their compulsion forces them to be rebels with neither cause nor clue and eventually you're going to make the local regime angry enough that you'll no longer find yourself very well accepted there.<br /> <br /> With Brujah Princes specifically I expect that their domains would be a little chaotic. When their compulsion would kick in and they'd have to do something unexpected or take a stand against some task that they had the responsibility of carrying out and until they did so their effectiveness would be reduced. Over time this would probably have given Brujah Princes the stereotype of being somewhat capricious and less than capable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-14-2021, 08:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T05:19:24-07:00","id":1456804,"title":"","content":"probably the same way as an inappropriate frenzy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-14T09:21:08-07:00","id":1456813,"title":"","content":"I imagine the clan stockpiles an impressive arsena